WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.762
Unit 3 is T L S inspection.

2
00:00:02.762 --> 00:00:06.618
It decrypts H T T P S at the
service edge, so full U R L's,

3
00:00:06.618 --> 00:00:12.260
files and content can be filtered, then
re-encrypts; it's the prerequisite

4
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:17.338
for U R L rules, file and content
policies, and A I prompt inspection.

5
00:00:17.338 --> 00:00:21.437
Learn offers a Microsoft-managed
certificate, or the agency's own.

6
00:00:21.437 --> 00:00:25.215
With the agency's own, the agency
signs an intermediate C A,

7
00:00:25.215 --> 00:00:29.313
and the service issues short-lived
leaf certificates from it.

8
00:00:29.313 --> 00:00:33.710
Learn's limits: valid at least six
months, only one active at a time,

9
00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:38.025
with server authentication and
the C A extensions Learn lists.

10
00:00:38.025 --> 00:00:39.013
Which C A?

11
00:00:39.013 --> 00:00:43.963
Learn's tutorial suggests a dedicated
C A, not your production P K I.

12
00:00:43.963 --> 00:00:48.685
The program issues it from a dedicated
issuing C A under the agency's root,

13
00:00:48.685 --> 00:00:53.250
never from the C A that issues
authentication certificates, because a

14
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:58.287
compromised inspection C A can impersonate
any site to every managed device.

15
00:00:58.287 --> 00:01:00.465
Deploy trust before activation:

16
00:01:00.465 --> 00:01:05.463
the root and intermediate go to clients
by Intune first, because an expired

17
00:01:05.463 --> 00:01:10.300
inspection certificate disables all
T L S inspection across the tenant.

18
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.530
Renew at least ninety days ahead.
